<title>ITALY: ALPINE SKIING-AUSTRIA'S FRANZ BREAKS WRIST.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-AUSTRIA'S FRANZ BREAKS WRIST.</headline>
<dateline>SESTRIERE, Italy 1997-02-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Austrian Werner Franz broke his left wrist and chipped a bone in his left heel after crashing in the downhill at the world ski championships on Saturday.</p>
<p>Werner Margreiter, head coach of the Austrian men's team, said Franz had also broken a bone in the same hand and would be out of competition for about two weeks.</p>
<p>&quot;He skied very badly at the top and he then took too many risks,&quot; said Margreiter.</p>
</text>
